cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use named-arrays in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: named-arrays
abstract: >-
  named-arrays is a Python implementation of a named tensor, an n-dimensional
  array whose axes are identified only by name. Arrays broadcast against each
  other by matching axis names, so singleton dimensions are never needed, and
  most of the NumPy API accepts axis names in place of indices. Values can
  carry physical units through astropy.units, and uncertain arrays propagate
  their uncertainty through every operation. The array types extend from
  scalars to vectors, matrices, and discrete functions, with support for
  plotting, random sampling, resampling onto curvilinear grids, and
  optimization.
authors:
